version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "[RELEASE DATE]"
abstract: "Computer-assisted proof candidates for Open Questions 6.2 and 6.4 of C. Gaiser, Restricted generalized Schur numbers (arXiv:2608.08789): S_3(k;2) = k^3+3k^2+2k-2 for every k >= 3; the exact thresholds K(3),...,K(11) = 3,4,6,7,8,9,10,11,12 (K(11)=12 new in v1.1); the two-colour weak Schur numbers WS_8(2)=365, WS_9(2)=505, WS_10(2)=676; and the asymptotic threshold K(l) = ((1+sqrt 2)/2) l + O(1), with (1+a)l-4 < K(l) < (1+a)l+5 for l >= 50, a=(sqrt 2-1)/2 (new in v1.2); K(19) >= 21, K(20) >= 22; new in v1.3: K(l) = l+1 for 12 <= l <= 18, K(19) = 21, K(20) = 22, S_2(20;19) = 4181, S_2(21;20) = 4861, a prefix-dominance lemma for the T1-fill template, and (1+a)l-3.63 < K(l) <= (1+a)l+16-11 sqrt 2 < (1+a)l+0.444 for l >= 19. Not peer reviewed."
keywords: ["Schur numbers", "Ramsey theory", "SAT", "LRAT", "Lean", "computer-assisted proof"]
license: CC-BY-4.0
